Stretch the view past the first or last column and bounce it back.

When focus-column-left/right or move-column-left/right can't go further, the
view quickly stretches towards the edge and bounces back.  Key repeats don't
bounce again, so holding the key bounces only once.  The new
`column-edge-bounce` animation configures the bounce back; `off` disables it.
Not upstream yet; this is the 26.04 backport of the change prepared for a niri
pull request.

