+#### `column-edge-bounce`
+
+<sup>Since: next release</sup>
+
+The view bouncing back after `focus-column-left`, `focus-column-right`, `move-column-left` or `move-column-right` stretched it past the first or last column.
+
+When one of these actions can't go further, the view quickly stretches towards the edge, then bounces back with this animation.
+Holding the key of the bind bounces only once.
+
+Set it to `off` to disable the stretch and the bounce.
+
+```kdl
+animations {
+    column-edge-bounce {
+        spring damping-ratio=1.0 stiffness=800 epsilon=0.0001
+    }
+}
+```
+
 #### `window-movement`
 
 <sup>Since: 0.1.5</sup>
